• unforeseen difficulties operating in new product areas or new geographic areas; and
• customer or key employee losses at the acquired businesses.
If we consummate any future acquisitions, our capitalization and results of operations may change significantly and our unitholders likely will not have the opportunity
to evaluate the economic, financial and other relevant information that we will consider in determining the application of these funds and other resources.
If we acquire assets that are distinct and separate from our existing terminalling, gathering and transportation operations, it could subject us to additional business and
operating risks.
